From: DBY-W09 contributors <dby-w09@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: sm8250: preserve TX codec DMA capture channels

Allow TX_CODEC_DMA_TX_3 to retain the channel interval negotiated by
ASoC. Its AFE and TX macro DAIs support up to eight channels and the
WCD938x capture DAI supports four; forcing stereo discards that range.
There is no DT property to override this machine-driver fixup.
Keep the stereo override for all other backends and retain the existing
48000 Hz and S16_LE fixups for every backend.

SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0
Signed-off-by: DBY-W09 contributors <dby-w09@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/sm8250.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/sm8250.c
@@ -65,7 +65,8 @@
 	struct snd_mask *fmt = hw_param_mask(params, SNDRV_PCM_HW_PARAM_FORMAT);

 	rate->min = rate->max = 48000;
-	channels->min = channels->max = 2;
+	if (snd_soc_rtd_to_cpu(rtd, 0)->id != TX_CODEC_DMA_TX_3)
+		channels->min = channels->max = 2;
 	snd_mask_set_format(fmt, SNDRV_PCM_FORMAT_S16_LE);

 	return 0;
